WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:35.990
<b>Sakura and the Fire and Water Birds</b>

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.900
It's a pop-up book, I see.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:55.380
It has so many movable parts.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.590
What do you think? Is it one 
that you've read before?

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:18.640
No, I have some pop-up books about Alice,

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.120
but I don't have this one.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.470
Glad to hear it!

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.430
That'll make Rika-chan happy, too.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:25.590
How's she doing?

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.610
Great! She said we should hang out, sometime.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:32.360
Oh, I need to return a book 
to her when I see her next.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:35.440
Does Rika-san like books, too?

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.000
Yeah.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:40.000
But I think she likes music even more.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.500
She's great at playing piano, 
and she has lots of piano scores.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:48.360
Oh, and she said she was learning 
to play the flute next.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.830
That suits her!

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:50.700
Uh-huh!

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:54.040
If I recall, she was learning to play 
the Paraguayan harp, too.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.290
She's good at many things, then!

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:56.940
Uh-huh!

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:00.620
I'm thinking of learning to 
play an instrument, too.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:02.280
Really? Which one?

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:03.770
The matryomin.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.030
You haven't heard of it?

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:06.780
No...

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.970
Have you heard of matryoshka dolls?

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.030
Uh-huh.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:13.180
You put one of those in front of you,

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:15.460
then you do this with your hands,

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.130
then you move them like this...

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.460
That's how you play it.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:26.120
Is it related to the theremin?

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:29.010
Right! It's like a relative of that.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:31.790
I have seen a theremin before.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:35.840
The outside can be basically anything,

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:38.030
<b>Matryomin</b>

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.320
so I'd like to make an original one.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:40.780
<b>Theremin</b>

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:39.340
What kind?

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:40.790
A kokeshi?

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.530
<b>Kokemin</b>

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.720
Don't make it too scary, okay?

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.660
<b>Keromin</b>

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:50.340
If it can be anything, maybe you could 
make it look like a mascot character?

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:49.270
What's the matter?

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.110
Nothing. I'm okay.

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:54.720
Like the one Akiho-chan always 
carries, Momo-chan.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:55.990
That's a good idea!

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:58.080
Your Kero-san could work, too!

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.530
Huh? Oh... Yeah, you're right.

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:02.000
Speaking of mascots,

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.770
that cooking lesson yesterday was crazy, huh?

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:05.370
<b>Gulp!</b>

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:08.760
After I worked so hard to make a roll 
cake that looked like my Maro...

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.660
That's your family's dog, right?

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:14.700
She showed us the latest pictures.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.910
Maro was as cute as ever!

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:20.300
Thanks! I wonder why the 
decorations disappeared, though...

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:20.530
<b>Gulp!</b>

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:21.060
<b>Gulp! Gulp!</b>

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:24.070
You hadn't made anything 
with them yet, right?

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:26.770
Didn't you all fall asleep afterward?

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:30.080
Yeah, but all the ingredients disappeared.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:30.290
<b>
Gulp!</b>

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:30.540
<b>
Gulp! Gulp!</b>

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.410
<b>
Gulp! Gulp! Gulp!</b>

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.400
It's strange, isn't it?

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.840
Wh-What is it, Naoko-chan?

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:41.810
I thought maybe I could use that in the 
script I'm writing for the Theater Club.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:42.950
Flump!

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.290
Sakura-san?

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:49.470
But the ones we remade still turned 
out cute, didn't they, Akiho-chan?

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:51.290
Yes.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.690
What did you make, Sakura-chan?

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:54.350
Huh?

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:57.230
U-Um...

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:01.230
After all that happened with the card,

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.770
it didn't come out quite the 
way I'd planned, but...

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:07.600
Here.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.050
I made it during our cooking lesson.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:11.890
For me?

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.500
Y-Yeah.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:20.670
Can I look at it now?

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.370
Huh? Uh, sure...

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:29.520
This is...

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:33.860
Th-The plan was to make your whole outfit,

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:36.810
but there weren't enough ingredients left.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:39.760
Sakura.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:40.610
Yes?

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:42.770
Thanks.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:46.790
Sakura-chan...

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:48.820
Your face is red.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.920
It looks like the person you care 
for most was pleased with it.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.470
Oh? Akiho-chan, you're red, too.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.010
W-Well, lunch break is almost over!

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:04.570
Oh, Sakura-san, thank you 
for showing me this book!

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:08.750
Rika-chan told me to give it to you.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:12.460
She said it would make her happy.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:14.290
I couldn't...

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:15.800
She insisted!

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:16.820
But...

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:21.080
I'm sure it would make her 
happier for you to keep it.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.780
Yeah, much happier!

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:25.740
Even better if you told her what 
you thought of the book!

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.760
Yes, definitely.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:30.980
Are you sure it's all right?

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:32.870
Uh-huh!

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.150
Thank you so much!

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:39.160
I'll make sure to give her my thoughts on it!

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:40.360
Yeah!

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:44.500
<i>Huh?</i>

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:10.390
Sakura-san!

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:13.250
Be careful where you step!

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:19.570
Are you all right? Do you feel sick?

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:23.450
No, I just spaced out a little.

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:27.740
Just wondering what I'd do if I 
were called on in math class.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.220
I did study, but...

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:52.470
An Alice book... should go right here.

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:03.580
Kaito-san!

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.880
Did I interrupt?

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:10.230
No, I was just putting away 
a book my friend gave me.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.030
A picture book about Alice?

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:13.250
Yes.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:16.640
I love all books, but in the end...

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.860
The ones about Alice are special?

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:20.880
Yes...

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.400
Especially,

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:31.340
<i>Alice in Clock Land?</i>

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:35.950
Kaito-san?

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:42.330
I was thinking of making some cocoa. 
Would you care for some?

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:44.770
Yes, I'll have some!

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:50.960
You could have used the internal line.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.880
I thought of doing that.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:56.340
But I suspected you might be too absorbed 
in your books to hear it, and...

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:00.800
I was a bit curious, as well.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:02.260
Curious?

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:07.000
When you came home from school, 
you seemed a bit down.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:08.760
Oh!

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.040
I-I'm sorry!

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:13.530
There's nothing you need to apologize for.

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:21.150
Sakura-san... seemed a little down, today.

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:23.820
Might she have taken ill?

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:26.460
It didn't seem that way.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:30.090
She just suddenly started spacing out.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:34.890
Almost as if her mind had 
gone away, somewhere...

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:48.870
Akiho-san?

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:51.830
I heard...

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:56.550
the sound of a clock...

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:59.000
Was it my pocket watch?

00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:03.620
No, it was a much, much... bigger.

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:11.280
It appears the clock in 
your belly is going off.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:14.830
Let's have dinner before I make that cocoa.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:16.560
O-Okay...

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:21.060
Akiho-san.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:23.690
Yes?

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:26.650
It's wonderful that your friend 
gave you that book.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.190
Yes!

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:35.310
I hope you can become even better 
friends with Sakura-san.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:45.290
<b>Tsukimine Shrine</b>

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:50.300
Beautiful! You look beautiful!

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:53.540
It's been so long since I've been 
able to film you in costume.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:55.040
Let's have a smile!

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:59.420
Here's your smile! Howzat?!

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:02.000
You look lovely, too, Kero-chan!

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.770
I know, right?

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:08.310
Since you're with us this time, 
Li-kun, you should join her.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:10.850
No, I...

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:17.740
<b>Tsukimine Shrine</b>

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:15.120
I can't believe ya sensed a 
card this late at night...

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:18.040
It does kinda bring back memories, though.

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:24.650
Now that you mention it, this was where 
I captured the first Clow Card, The Fly.

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:25.950
That's true...

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:30.030
This is basically the birthplace 
of Cardcaptor Sakura!

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:35.130
Come to think of it, you were pretty 
pushy when we first met.

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:39.280
You just suddenly popped 
out of that book and...

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:43.420
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:46.700
And then, you kept talking and talking.

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:51.840
Then he up and said, "Witness the 
birth of the Cardcaptor!"

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:56.560
Also, the cards were scattered 
because <i>he</i> fell asleep.

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.890
But all he said was, "Stuff happens!"

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:04.210
And just so you know, I never 
agreed to get into this!

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:06.470
Was that how it happened?

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:07.770
Yes, it was!

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:13.690
The Fly was huge, so I jumped 
on, out of desperation,

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:18.460
but now that I think about it, 
what if I had fallen off?

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.650
But ya didn't fall off!

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:22.960
Precisely why I never had a doubt about you.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:25.170
I just got lucky, that's all!

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:28.020
Well, if ya had fallen, 
I woulda had your back—

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:30.590
You were blown away, right at the start!

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:34.890
If Sakura-chan had refused to help you,

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:37.010
would it have dissolved the contract?

00:12:37.010 --> 00:12:38.360
Nope!

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:39.610
That's harsh...

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:42.260
Well, once a magic contract is formed,

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:45.880
it can't be broken, unless something 
really serious happens.

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:49.280
So there's no cooling-off period?

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:51.370
That really is harsh.

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:18.950
What do you feel?

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.320
I think it's a card.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:30.440
That's hot!

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:32.380
Its wind burns!

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:42.170
We have to hurry!

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:44.260
Kero-chan, protect Tomoyo-chan!

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:44.930
Right!

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:47.400
Tomoyo, this way!

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:48.090
Okay!

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:52.510
Sakura-chan...

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:56.230
Make absolutely sure you don't 
do anything reckless.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:58.480
I don't want you getting hurt!

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:02.230
Okay! Same to you, Sakura-chan!

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:09.550
I'm a fire type, too,

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:12.480
so anything I do would be like 
throwin' oil on a flame...

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:19.130
Water, rain down upon the fire bird!

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:20.500
<i>Aqua!</i>

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:41.350
That's it! Give 'em what for!

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:53.470
How can we...

00:14:54.650 --> 00:14:56.070
I'll try!

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:59.280
Syaoran-kun!

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:05.120
Sakura, use Flight's magic to get 
as close to the bird as you can,

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:08.440
so you can turn it into a card, 
as soon as it falters.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:09.860
Right!

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:16.730
Take me closer to the fire bird!

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:21.420
<i>Flight!</i>

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:00.050
Wow.

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:02.350
Now, Sakura!

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:04.530
Right!

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:07.290
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:11.260
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:13.970
<i>Secure!</i>

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:37.350
<b>Blaze</b>

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:37.300
"Blaze"...

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:40.910
Blaze.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:47.520
Syaoran-kun! Tomoyo-chan! Kero-chan!

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:49.580
You okay, Sakura?

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:50.610
Yeah!

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.900
You both performed splendidly.

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:55.410
It's all thanks to you, Syaoran-kun!

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:56.300
Huh?

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:58.540
That wind magic was amazing!

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:00.830
Or was it a technique?

00:17:04.030 --> 00:17:07.790
Boy, I sure am glad you got 
it turned into a card.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:08.670
Yeah.

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:11.300
Fire magic, huh?

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:17.480
So now we know this new set of cards 
has wind, water, and fire, too.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:22.110
Yeah, but this one was really intense.

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:26.180
Those two birds were blasting each 
other with their water and flames!

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:29.920
Yeah, sorta like a giant monster battle, huh?

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:33.320
More like it <i>was</i> a giant monster battle.

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:34.190
Yeah.

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:36.520
It's too bad, though...

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:39.130
If the new card had been a water type,

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:42.410
I coulda helped out with my own flames!

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:44.200
I'm not sure I could trust that.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:44.750
Harsh!

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.110
That's mean, Sakura!

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:50.860
I was kidding. I trust you. 
I trust you, okay?

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:52.150
Hmph!

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:57.290
But still, Sakura, didn't you say it'd be 
better to have 'em show up at night

00:17:57.290 --> 00:18:03.560
than to have cakes jumpin' around or trees 
walkin' freely at school in the morning?

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:07.160
I did, but it was still just 
as tough to deal with.

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:10.300
Either way, you dealt with it handily,

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:12.410
in true Cardcaptor form!

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:13.690
That's right.

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:22.830
<b>Tsukimine Shrine</b>

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:17.250
The arch got a little burned,

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:19.740
but I'm glad a fire didn't break out.

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:22.130
We'd better head back.

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.810
I'm fine since I live alone,

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:27.580
but if you two are out late...

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:31.080
I arranged a few things in advance, 
so I should be all right.

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:34.960
Someone's gonna catch on 
to ya, sooner or later...

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:39.700
I've always left through my window like 
that when someone else was home.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:41.210
Yeah, but leavin' <i>that</i>?

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:46.810
I have a bodyguard waiting for us nearby.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:51.850
As soon as you're both done changing, 
I'll have you driven home.

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:53.390
Quietly.

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:54.660
Thanks.

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:05.780
What's wrong, Toya?

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:10.410
Toya?

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:20.000
Sakura-chan must have gone to bed.

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:24.410
H-Hey... Toya!

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:43.820
She thought this would cover it up?

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:48.840
And it doesn't even occur to her 
to use that power of hers?

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:58.920
You shouldn't go into a girl's 
room without permission.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.150
She's not in there.

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:05.720
Looks like she and that yellow 
plushie took off again.

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:20.780
This is sudden.

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:26.240
Well, Dad isn't home today, 
so that's no problem.

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:29.500
Master will return home soon.

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:32.140
How do you know?

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:33.410
I sense her.

00:20:33.780 --> 00:20:35.240
That's handy.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:38.950
But sometimes, I cannot sense it...

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:45.230
There are times when I cannot trace 
the mark of my master's power.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:47.620
What times?

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:50.600
I can identify no regularity.

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:55.730
Even though her power's gotten 
so strong, even I can sense it?

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:02.610
Your power has started to return, hasn't it?

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:06.520
What will you use that power for?

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:08.900
I won't say it yet.

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:09.970
Why?

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:13.600
Didn't I tell you before that you 
and Yuki are a lot alike?

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:17.210
Yes, though I cannot agree.

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:20.640
I guess not.

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:24.730
It's my power.

00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:28.430
I'll decide how I use it. And when.

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:32.550
You're so easy to read.

00:21:32.550 --> 00:21:33.870
How do you mean?

00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:36.310
When you're angry or upset,

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:40.180
it shows on your face, 
even if you don't say it.

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:41.940
No...

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.820
Yuki told me your name.

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:49.310
Oh, don't be mad at him.

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:54.550
It seemed wrong not knowing your name, 
having known you for so long.

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:56.290
So I asked him.

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.210
I cannot rebuke him in person.

00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:02.500
Good point.

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:13.010
I'll do whatever I can for 
my family... for Sakura.

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:15.670
That's the one thing I'm sure about.

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:20.190
I know that.

00:22:22.350 --> 00:22:25.900
So just wait a little longer, Yue.

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:12.130
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:19.640
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:19.640
<b>K</b>

00:24:13.090 --> 00:24:16.760
Brought to you with burning passion and cool 
wisdom, it's "Leave It to Kero-chan!"

00:24:16.760 --> 00:24:19.640
Today, naturally, I'm introducin' 
another battle costume!

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:22.940
This exotic outfit matches a flame design

00:24:22.940 --> 00:24:25.230
with harem pants, hair ornament, 
chest, waist, and nail bijoux.

00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:27.180
The bangles are a subtle, 
but effective, touch.

00:24:27.180 --> 00:24:30.740
Tomoyo never runs short on variation. 
Wish she'd make more for me, too...

00:24:29.740 --> 00:24:30.740
<b>"Bijou" is French for "jewel"!</b>

00:24:30.740 --> 00:24:33.380
The back gate, where she captured that 
card, brought back memories, huh?

00:24:30.740 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:30.740 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>K</b>

00:24:33.380 --> 00:24:36.040
Bet ya could fry a ton of okonomiyaki 
with that card's flames.

00:24:36.040 --> 00:24:38.360
I'll have Sakura try it, so we can 
test our limits, sometime.

00:24:38.360 --> 00:24:39.990
Ta-ta!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.000
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:40.270 --> 00:24:44.460
I'll be going with Yukito-san 
to help him read to kids.

00:24:44.460 --> 00:24:47.240
I invited Akiho-chan and Syaoran-kun, too!

00:24:47.240 --> 00:24:48.700
I'm so excited!

00:24:48.950 --> 00:24:51.900
Next time, "Sakura and Akiho's Lullaby."

00:24:48.960 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura and Akiho's Lullaby</b>

00:24:51.900 --> 00:24:54.840
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>End</b>
